{#
  Wraps an existing form group so govuk-frontend's character count attaches to it.

  Used with {% call %} so the field's own markup is untouched:

      {% from "_character-count.njk" import characterCount %}
      {% call characterCount(500, characterCountMessages) %}
        <div class="govuk-form-group">
          <label ...>
          <textarea class="govuk-textarea govuk-js-character-count" maxlength="500" ...></textarea>
        </div>
      {% endcall %}

  🔴 Deliberately NOT the `govukCharacterCount` macro. That macro GENERATES the label,
  hint, textarea and error message from parameters, so adopting it would mean rewriting
  every field's markup — and these fields are hand-written, with their own ids, hints,
  required flags and error wiring that existing tests assert on. This emits the same
  wrapper the macro emits and leaves the field alone.

  🔴 The textarea inside MUST carry `govuk-js-character-count`, and SHOULD keep its
  `maxlength`. The class is how the component finds the field. Keeping `maxlength` means
  the browser still enforces the limit when JavaScript does not run — the count is an
  enhancement, not the enforcement.

  `messages` is `res.locals.characterCountMessages`; without it the component announces
  govuk-frontend's built-in ENGLISH strings to speakers of all eleven languages.
#}
{% macro characterCount(maxlength, messages, textareaId) %}
<div class="govuk-character-count" data-module="govuk-character-count" data-maxlength="{{ maxlength }}"
  {%- if messages %}
    {%- for pluralRule, message in messages.under %} data-i18n.characters-under-limit.{{ pluralRule }}="{{ message | escape }}"{% endfor %}
    {%- if messages.at %} data-i18n.characters-at-limit="{{ messages.at | escape }}"{% endif %}
    {%- for pluralRule, message in messages.over %} data-i18n.characters-over-limit.{{ pluralRule }}="{{ message | escape }}"{% endfor %}
  {%- endif %}>
  {{ caller() }}
  {#
    🔴 REQUIRED. govuk-frontend throws an ElementError if `{textareaId}-info` is absent,
    and writes its own ENGLISH allowance text into it if it is empty. Populating it with
    a translated sentence prevents both. The component moves this element to sit directly
    after the textarea and hides it visually, using it as the field's description.
  #}
  <div id="{{ textareaId }}-info" class="govuk-hint govuk-character-count__message">{{ messages.describe(maxlength) if messages else "" }}</div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
